<p><strong>Disclosure:</strong> this guide is published by the maker of Cortisol+. It compares official documentation we checked on September 16, 2026.</p>
<p>It is not a hands-on ranking, an independent review or a clinical accuracy study.</p>

<h2>Which Apple Watch stress app should you consider?</h2>
<p><strong>Start with what you want to understand.</strong> That might be your HRV in the moment, a day of stress readings, or how sleep and recovery link up.</p>
<p>Having more sensors doesn't make one score "best" for everyone. What matters is how the app explains things, how it handles missing data, and how it fits your routine.</p>

