<h2>Which Welltory alternative fits your routine?</h2>
<p><strong>Cortisol+, StressWatch, Bevel and Athlytic are all options to compare for Apple Watch stress tracking.</strong></p>
<p>Cortisol+ shows a weighted wellness score with HRV and sleep context. StressWatch focuses on stress trends and how they look on the Watch. Bevel describes a stress timeline next to other health features. Athlytic describes recovery and exertion tools for training.</p>
<p>Choose by the information you'll actually use. This review of documentation doesn't show which is most accurate.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>To understand the inputs behind a daily score:</strong> explore <a href="/how-it-works/">Cortisol+'s published methodology</a> and <a href="/stress/apple-watch/#walkthrough">recorded app walkthrough</a>.</li>
  <li><strong>To follow stress trends on your wrist:</strong> compare <a href="https://stresswatch.app/">StressWatch's trend views and Watch widgets</a> with what your plan includes.</li>
  <li><strong>To see a stress timeline:</strong> <a href="https://www.bevel.health/blog/stress-monitor">Bevel explains how it reads heart rate, HRV and movement</a>, including time spent at different score levels.</li>
  <li><strong>To plan workouts around recovery:</strong> <a href="https://athlyticapp.com/getting-started/">Athlytic describes its recovery, exertion and sleep views</a>. Its recovery score and stress view do different jobs.</li>
  <li><strong>To look at the raw data first:</strong> Apple Health is a good place to start before paying for another subscription. Follow our <a href="/hrv/apple-watch/">Apple Watch HRV guide</a>.</li>
</ul>

<ZenTip image="/app-ui/zen_presenting_new.webp">
  Pick the app whose explanation you <strong>actually understand</strong>. A score you can't explain is hard to use.
</ZenTip>

<h2>What is the best cortisol tracking app for Apple Watch?</h2>
<p><strong>There is no proven accuracy winner here.</strong> We reviewed documented features, not a clinical head-to-head test.</p>
<p>For wearable stress tracking, choose the app whose explanation and workflow make sense to you. For a hormone level, use a proper test, not an app score.</p>
<p>Our <a href="/cortisol/track/#cortisol-tracking-app">cortisol tracking app guide</a> separates these options and explains free versus subscription access.</p>

