<h2 id="same-day-check">A same-day comparison you can actually record</h2>
<p><strong>Compare apps on the same day, with the same device.</strong> For each app, write down:</p>
<ul>
  <li>the app version and the time window you picked</li>
  <li>the latest underlying sample, and any missing readings</li>
  <li>the score shown and how the app explains it</li>
  <li>the price and renewal period offered to your account</li>
</ul>
<p>If these details differ, a difference between scores is not a fair accuracy test.</p>
<p><strong>Our evidence limit:</strong> we checked the linked descriptions. We have not run this test across all the apps. We don't claim a winner, a measured setup time or a clinical accuracy advantage.</p>
<p>The <a href="/stress/apple-watch/#walkthrough">Cortisol+ app walkthrough</a> shows our product. It is not evidence about other apps.</p>
<p><a href="/resources/apple-watch-app-checklist/">Use the free eight-check app comparison worksheet</a> to keep these notes together. Download the blank CSV and record what you find.</p>

<h2>What should I ask during a trial?</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Can I see the underlying readings and when they were recorded?</li>
  <li>Does the app explain missing data and how it builds my baseline?</li>
  <li>Can I tell the difference between workout strain and how I feel mentally?</li>
  <li>Are the features I need included in the price shown to me?</li>
  <li>Can I understand and control how my data is shared?</li>
</ol>
<p>Use your own account's current offer to compare prices and renewal periods. We haven't copied each app's current paywall, and we don't show price ranges we haven't checked.</p>

<h2>Which one measures cortisol?</h2>
<p><strong>None of these wearable stress apps give a lab cortisol measurement.</strong></p>
<p>Cortisol+'s number comes from a model, and we have not shown its clinical accuracy against hormone testing. Calling something a "cortisol score" doesn't change that.</p>

